Updated Tcl/Tk Interface for the NExS Spreadsheet
- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Release Date: 2/9/97

X Engineering Software Systems (XESS Corp.) announces the immediate
availability of an updated Tcl/Tk interface to its NExS spreadsheet.

The tclNExS package provides a Tcl/Tk interface to the NExS conNExions API.
It provides a powerful graphical scripting environment for adding
user-defined features and functions to the NExS spreadsheet. The network
extensible features of NExS are included in tclNExS, facilitating
development of distributed network NExS applications. Example scripts are
included which demonstrate user-defined @-functions and menus, real-time
spreadsheet data feeds, and batch-mode spreadsheet processing.

The 1.0.2 release includes pre-built binaries for all supported NExS
platforms (AIX, Digital Unix, HPUX, Linux, Solaris, and SunOS), as well as
complete source code and documentation. The binaries included in the package
are based on the most recent stable version of Tcl/Tk, Tcl7.6/Tk4.2.

Improvements made in release 1.0.2 include:

   * Removal of 32-bit pointer dependencies that prevented tclNExS from
     running properly on 64-bit machines (i.e., DEC Alpha).

   * The cdisp.tcl script now produces correct code when building with Tcl
     7.5 or later.

   * The mknexsAppInit script (which auto-detects the version of wish on the
     system during the build) has been updated to work correctly with
     versions of Tk from 3.6 to 4.2.

Those interested in the updated tclNExS package can download it from
www.xess.com. A free, 30-day version of the NExS spreadsheet and the new
conNExions-BETA API can also be downloaded for the HP/UX, AIX, Digital UNIX,
SunOS, Solaris and Linux platforms.

