The first non-beta version of the dmsdos filesystem driver has just been
released.

The dmsdos filesystem mounts doublespace, drivespace and stacker compressed
dos volumes read-write. In detail:

	- Dos 6.0, 6.2 Doublespace
	- Dos 6.22 Drivespace
	- Win95 Doublespace/Drivespace
	- Win95 Drivespace 3 from Plus! pack (without 'ultra' compression)
	- Stacker 3 (write access without compression)
	- Stacker 4

Improvements since 0.7.5:

	- again more speed, especially on write access
	- more kernels supported
	- bugfixes, of course

>From the documentation:
	"0.8.0 is first non-beta release of the dmsdos filesystem. It does
	 not mean that the code is guaranteed to contain no bugs, but it 
	 does mean that it is supposed to be ready for daily use. It does not 
	 mean that you needn't backup important data before using this driver,
	 but it does mean that you very likely never need your backup. :-) "

If you cannot find it on the ftp servers listed below, try the incoming
directories.

Frank


Begin3
Title:		dmsdosfs
Version:	0.8.0
Entered-date:	06FEB97
Description:	dmsdos filesystem for Linux: extends msdos filesystem to allow
                full read and restricted write access to msdos/win95 compressed
                partitions (msdos files like dblspace.xxx and drvspace.xxx and
                stacvol.xxx). The following configurations are supported:
                 - DoubleSpace / DriveSpace compressed msdos 6.x partitions
                   (read-write, fully supported),
                 - DoubleSpace / DriveSpace compressed win95 partitions
                   (read-write, fully supported),
                 - DriveSpace 3 (from Plus! pack) compressed win95 partitions
                   (read-write, without Ultra compression method support),
                 - Stacker 3 compressed partitions (read-write, but write
                   access currently without compression),
                 - Stacker 4 compressed partitions (read-write)
                *** It does NOT support new FAT32 filesystems. ***
                Dmsdos can run together with vfat or umsdos and can handle 
                win95 long filenames itself.
                This version preferres a Linux kernel >= 2.0.1. Older kernels
                except 1.2.13 are not supported (untested).
                Support for 2.1.x kernels has been added, but it may not work 
                with brand new kernels. Using dmsdos as a module in newer 
                2.1.x kernels may not work (untested).
Keywords:	filesystem compression doublespace drivespace stacker
Author: 	gockel@etecs4.uni-duisburg.de (Frank Gockel)
                pisa@cvlinux.felk.cvut.cz (Pavel Pisa)
