We are pleased to announce that the source code of the Thot structured
editor is now available by anonymous ftp.
Several binaries may also be downloaded for various Unix platforms.

You can get Thot version 2.0b at the following URL:
http://opera.inrialpes.fr/thot/

Overview
- --------
Thot Editor is a structured document editor, offering a graphical WYSIWYG
interface under X-Windows. Thot offers the usual functionality of a
word processor, but it also processes the document structure. It
includes a large set of advanced tools, such as a spell checker and
an index generator, and it allows to export documents to common
formats like HTML and LaTeX.

The editor is based on a the Thot library, which is a generic system for
the development of document centered applications based on the concept of 
structured active documents. It can be used for building interactive system
as well as automatic processors.

The Thot library is also the basis on which Amaya, the W3C browser/editor,
has been built.

Contributions
- -------------
If you are interested in participating in the development of Thot, please
contact the Opera project (Cecile.Roisin@inrialpes.fr)

For more information, see Opera project pages (http://opera.inrialpes.fr)
and Amaya pages (http://www.w3.org/pub/WWW/Amaya).

