Title:          Universal MIME Plug-in for Netscape
Version:        1.1
Entered-date:   February 11, 1997
Description:    This is a Universal (I hope) MIME plug-in for Linux.
Basically, given a configuration file, it registers the plug-in with a
corresponding MIME type.  For each MIME type, there must be associated
extension(s) and command line to run.  For instance, given the
MIME type audio/x-midi, it would register with Netscape that it can
handle embedded files with the .mid extensions.  Of course, a program
like playmidi is required to play the file.  Take a look at the sample
configuration file for examples of how to configure the plug-in.

This program was developed to play embedded midi and wav music.  Since
it requires seperate programs to actually play the file, it does not
support streaming.  Nor does it have the funky midi and wav controls
seen in the Windows version of Netscape, although I would like to add
them eventually.

Keywords:       plugin netscape midi wav linux
