Hi Unix-Gamers!

As some bugs have found their way into XBlast 2.2, I just 
have uploaded an update for XBlast 2.2 to XBlast 2.2.1, which 
help you to get rid of them. You can just retrieve the update
from:

ftp.x.org:       /contrib/games/multiplayer/xblast-2.2-to-2.2.1.tar.gz
sunsite.unc.edu: /pub/Linux/games/X11/video/xblast-2.2-to-2.2.1.tar.gz

WHAT IS XBLAST?

XBlast is a multi-player arcade game for X11R5/R6. The game can be
played with at least two players and up to four players. It can use one
to four X displays for output. XBlast supports color and monochrome
graphics. It was inspired by the video/computer game Bomberman
(Dynablaster), which was to my knowledge first programmed for NEC's PC
Engine/Turbo Grafx. Other (commercial) versions of the original game
exist for IBM-PC, Atari ST, Amiga, NES, GameBoy and Super NES.

WHATS NEW IN V2.2.1

 o "name bug" in Interactive Setup, when using fork mode removed.
   Fork mode is now saved to setup files

 o DSP sound mode queried by Interactive Setup (Linux)
   DSP sound setup saved to setup file

 o The Button extra is now distributed, right after taking it.

 o Star extras (invincibility) are now cumulative.

 o XBlast now allocates a private colormap, if necassary.

 o Window title now displays players' names.

 o Colors for player #6 are changed
 
 o  added F31 as stop key (needed for some Solaris machines)

 o Added template level-file "level-edit/Template.h" and put addLevel script
   back into the distribution.


PLATFORMS

It should compile on almost any UN*X with X11R5/R6.  XBlast 2.0 was
tested under Linux, HPUX, Ultrix, SunOS, Solaris, NetBSD and IRIX.
Older version were known to run under OSF, AIX, LynxOS.



Have fun blasting,

	Oliver Vogel

