                  Release of ypserv 1.1.5
                  =======================

Version 1.1.5 of an YP (NIS version 2) Server for Linux is released.
It also runs under SunOS 4.1.x, Solaris 2.x, AIX, HP-UX, IRIX, Ultrix 
and OSF1 (alpha).

The programs are needed to turn your workstation in a NIS server. 
It contains ypserv, ypxfr, rpc.ypxfrd, yppush, ypinit, revnetgroup, 
makedbm and /var/yp/Makefile.

This is NOT an NIS+ (NIS version 3) Server !

ypserv 1.1.5 is available under the GNU General Public License.

If you use a ypserv version prior to 1.1.4 as NIS master, you
should upgrade. Old versions of ypserv creates corrupted maps
and send wrong timestamps to your NIS slaves. After installing
ypserv 1.1.5 und generating the maps new on the master, you should 
delete the maps on your slaves and get them new from the master, 
or some maps will never be updated.

You could get the latest version from:

