Hello net,
 
after a long period of silence, we are now proud to issue a new version
of our popular program
 
        DOC++ version 3.0
 
This is a tool for producing both, online browsable HTML and
high quality hardcopy documentation for C, C++ and Java programs
directly from the source code.  It can be retreived from
 
        http://www.zib.de/Visual/software/doc++/index.html
        ftp://ftp.zib.de/pub/vispar/software/doc++/
 
This release involved a major redesign and reimplementation,
that includes many of the suggestions we had from our users.
Thanks to all for helping us to improve DOC++.
 
Major improvements/changes are:
 
     -  JavaDoc style documentation comments:
        This is the most severe change with respect to former releases.
        We replaced the @-comments from previous releases with JavaDoc
        /** ... */ comments.  Only exception: /// ...
 
     -  To support the transition from old DOC++ comments to the new format,
        we provided a simple utility that helps with that.  With its help
        switching to the new format took about 3/4 hour for 2 MB of code.
        Its name is ``promote'' and it must be called in a rather unintuitive
        manner:
 
        cat <oldfile> | promote | promote > <newfile>
 
     -  Inclusion of a Java parser.
 
     -  Support for HTML syntax for formating the documentation.
 
Thanks again to all for the encouraging feedback and bug-reports!
Good luck, your
 
        DOC++ Team      (doc++@zib.de)


