Announcing xldlas v0.80 
=======================

	I have recently placed version 0.80 of xldlas 
	in sunsite's incoming directory:

		ftp://sunsite.unc.edu/pub/Linux/Incoming/xldlas-0.80-source.tgz

	I expect it to be moved to:

		ftp://sunsite.unc.edu/pub/Linux/X11/xapps/math/xldlas-0.80-source.tgz

	shortly. It's also available on the xldlas homepage:

		http:/a42.com/~thor/xldlas

	You can find precomplied static and shared binaries there as well.


What's New
==========

	* A Test Menu (equality of means, sign)

	* A Filter Menu (outlier removal, detrending)

	* Some bug fixes (eg. no more integer rounding of median and quartiles)

What is it?
===========

	It's for doing statistics.


Highlights
==========


	* Based on the xforms library (ie. looks pretty slick)

	* Point and click interface to statistical summaries, OLS
	  regression, plotting, correlation analysis, etc.

	* Neural network and Genetic Algorithm data fitting
	  with some nice visual feedback.

	* Very handy automatic generating of .tex format and html 
	  log files, including tables and plots.

	* Online help



Where'd the Name come from
==========================

	xldlas was inspired by a non-X statistics program called ldlas,
        which stood for ldlas, damned lies, and statistics. So, I guess
	xldlas stands for x ldlas, damned lies, and statisitics.


ATTN: People Using Non-Linux OS's
=================================

	I'm looking for people to act as maintainers of pre-compiled
	non-Linux binaries of xldlas. Please see the web page for
	details.

Feedback
========

	The author (Thor Sigvaldason) is happy to receive feedback 
	at: thor@netcom.ca

LSM
