I am hoping it will be moved into the
/pub/Linux/utils/disk-management directory.

			---

cdchanger / tkchanger


cdchanger is an extension of the example program in the documentation
file for the IDE-CDROM driver which allows a program to change slots
of an ATAPI cdrom changer.

It is a setuid (root) program,  and thus can mount and unmount as
appropriate.  In normal operation (assuming the current device is
mounted) when a new slot is requested the device is unmounted and the
mount point and options saved.  After switching to the new slot the
device is remounted.

************************************************************************
NOTE:  This requires a fairly recent kernel, requiring changes to the
IDE CDROM driver, which went in version 2.1.9 I believe.
************************************************************************


		tkchanger

A companion program, tkchanger, is a perl/Tk interface to cdchanger.
It display a little window with a circle for each slot, in different
colours showing whether the slot is empty or has a disk, and which the
current disk is.  Simply click in the circle to make that the current
slot (which usually automatically unmounts and remounts the device).




