I have released dhcpcd-0.5. The following lists all the bug fixes and new 
features added in this release:

  1. IP multicast will be enabled when clients get an IP address.
  2. dhcpcd will not core-dump when it received a datagram containing
     the DHCP message option.
  3. added -r option which makes dhcpcd RFC1541 compliant.
  4. syslog messages now contain the dhcpcd's pid.
  5. changed the host information file name from "hostinfo" to
     "hostinfo-<ifname>" where <ifname> is replaced with the network 
     interface name like "eth0". This is good when multiple dhcpcd
     daemons are attached to different network interfaces.
  6. fixed dhcpcd so that it will not automatically exit when a sendto
     system call fails in the RENEWING state (note that this failure
     happens only when the server is down during the RENEWING state).
     This fix will prevent hosts from using expired IP addresses that
     are not properly released by dhcpcd when it exited prematurely
     without re-initializing the network interface.

The following is its LSM file:

