Administrivia:

CLUE welcomes members of the Linux User Community to speak at the monthly
   meetings.  Please contact president@clue.denver.co.us to arrange
   your talk.  All speakers are expected to provide a written summary of
   the talk so that we may place it in the newsletter and on our Web site.

CLUE has a home page!  Find us at http://www.clue.denver.co.us.
 
The CLUE Board of Directors meets immediately after the main Users
   Group meeting to schedule and organize the CLUE meetings and other
   Linux related activities.  The Board meeting is open to the public, 
   but attendees should note anyone who voices opinions may also be assigned 
   organizational responsibilities!  Volunteerism is a good thing!
   Feel free to stop by and observe sliently without risk, too!  :-)

   The location of the Board meeting will be announced at the February
   meeting.

CLUE is open to and actively seeks cooperative efforts with other
   User Groups in the Colorado Front Range and around the world.  Contact
   president@clue.denver.co.us to see what we can do together.

CLUE is a vendor independent, non-profit organization that was originally 
   founded by Mark Bolzern, President of WGS, and Rich Maginn, who was a 
   teacher at Smoky Hill High School at the time.  WGS and Smoky Hill High
   School continue to be proud supporters of CLUE but are not involved 
   in the administration of CLUE.  CLUE encourages vendor participation
   through the contribution of door prizes, topical presentations, and 
   software library contributions.

Getting on or off the CLUE Newsletter mailing list
   To subscribe to the CLUE Newsletter send email to 
   clue-newsletter-request@spot.elfwerks.com with the following as the 
   first line of text:

      subscribe clue-newsletter Your Name

	To unsubscribe, send email to clue-newsletter-request@spot.elfwerks.com
   with the following as the first line of text:

      unsubscribe clue-newsletter

   This information is also available at:
   http://www.clue.denver.co.us/~clue/newsletters/newsletter-subscribe.html


