                The BitWizard device driver service.

LINUX

    Many engineers are attracted to Linux because they use it at home.
    Putting Linux in a production environment however often stops at
    the boss' question "but is there support" and "is our hardware
    supported"?

ANNOUNCING

    BitWizard is pleased to annouce that it is starting a Linux-device
    driver service. This means that you can concentrate on creating PC
    based systems, and we will make the required device drivers for
    the cards that you select. In general, the driver will be ready
    within a week or two after we get the hardware and the
    documentation.

SUPPORT

    Many DOS device drivers that you get with a card are "black
    boxes".  We help opening these up. You'll get the source code to
    the device driver that you purchase. You have the source code to
    the operating system. This allows you to track possbile problems
    and resolve them.  We'll support you while you're developping your
    application.

    And we DO give support. Ever heard "We'll call you back" and never
    hear from them again? Not with us. Either we give you an immediate
    answer or we'll get back to you. Afraid of converting from DOS to
    Linux? Don't be afraid. We'll help.  Do you need support on the
    whole Linux system? We also have support contracts.

WHY LINUX?

    Do you need a rock-solid operating system, good development
    utilities, multitasking etc etc. Linux is a good choice. Doing a
    larger project under Linux is also very efficient: you create a
    few small applications that do the basic device interaction (when
    appropriate these come with the device driver), and you can put
    them together using scripts. If you need even better performance,
    you do the development using the scripts, and write the final
    application in one swoop in C or C++.

WHY USE THE DEVICE DRIVER SERVICE?

    The boss is interested in productivity and won't like you to spend
    an unknown time on developing device drivers. I hope that you will
    be able to convince your boss that Linux is an excellent choice
    now that you can buy the device drivers. We will do some research
    and make you a fixed-price offer, so you won't have to take the
    risk of the development taking more time than expected.

WHY BITWIZARD?

    We have extensive experience in writing device drivers. The goal
    of a device driver is to make life easier for the application
    programmers.  We'll really keep that in mind. We will give support
    on the products that we deliver. We will tell you in advance what
    it will cost you. We will tell you in advance when the product
    will be ready.

CONCLUSION

    Linux is an ideal platform for software development. If you don't
    want to take the risk of developing device drivers yourself, just
    contact us, and we will see what we can do for you.


                                        info@BitWizard.nl
