	Best Selling Dictionary & Thesaurus Now on Linux!

	DUX Software Corporation, a multi-platform software publisher
        since 1990, has announced the release of the Linux version of
        the best selling electronic dictionary, The Deluxe American
        Heritage Dictionary with Roget's II Thesaurus. This
        long-awaited release is ideal for tech writers, authors and
        researchers. Previously available only on PC's, the product
        offers the ultimate reference tool for UNIX users, with full
        definitions for well over 200,000 words, plus  pronunciations,
        derivations, proper usage, idioms and sample sentences. Single
        user, network, and site licenses are available for most UNIX
        platforms including Linux, Solaris, SCO, HPUX, AIX, and SGI.
- -----------------------------------------------------------------------
FEATURE LIST OF THE AMERICAN HERITAGE DICTIONARY AND ROGET'S THESAURUS

MAJOR FEATURES:

o 220,000 word Dictionary plus integrated 500,000 word Thesaurus
o Simple point and click Graphical User Interface (GUI)
o Scrolling windows
o Highly interactive and intuitive on the desktop
o On-line documentation
o Powerful Search characteristics
o Fast look-ups
o Auto Look-up with copy-paste function

Additional features include WordSearch, which allows search facilities
for almost any subject including thousands of famous personalities and
places. The Browse feature allows browsing of the entire dictionary from
A to Z. If the word is on the tip of your tongue, but you don't know the
entire spelling, the WildCard feature helps you find it fast. Anagram
provides words hidden in the one you are using. The renowned Roget's
II Thesaurus, is integrated with the dictionary and is highly
interactive with the dictionary's functions, allowing the user to flip
from a definition to its list of synonyms; and then to the synonym's
definition adding certainty that you are using the correct sense and
meaning.

An intuitive and colorful GUI lets the user point and click a function
or scroll the lists. Words can be entered into the dictionary's look-up
entry window, via the copy/paste function, from other applications
running on the desktop.  Part or all of the dictionary's definition
window text can be copied back into the text of editors, e-mail, word
processors, browsers, or major electronic publishing applications such
as FrameMaker.

Interested parties may download unlockable demonstration versions of
DUX's applications available at its web site http://www.dux.com.

THE DICTIONARY

Now you can have the benefits of the best selling electronic dictionary
on UNIX. The 200,000 word Deluxe Edition is the first completely new
dictionary for the '90s and the first full featured dictionary and
thesaurus on Linux.

Containing nearly twice as many words as the Standard Edition,  it is
one of the largest and most authoritative software dictionaries you can
buy.

The Liveliest New Dictionary In A Decade:

The Third Edition is the most current dictionary available
today--completely updated to keep pace with our colorful and ever
changing language.  It features up-to-the-minute definitions for new
words like ergonomics,  perestroika,  golden handcuffs,  CD-ROM, Pixel,
nonself,  Privatize,  and thousands more.

You Can Search More Than 200,000 Words And Get...

        Full definitions
        Parts of speech
        Pronunciation
        Proper usage
        Hyphenation
        Idioms
        Inflections
        Abbreviations
        Sample sentences
        Word origins (etymologies)

You'll also find biographical data on more than 8,000 individuals,
13,000 geographical entrees,  colleges and universities,  usage notes,
Indo-European roots, and more.  The software will even guide you to the
correct entry if you misspell the word you're trying to find.

OTHER NEW FEATURES:

WordSearch(TM)

WordSearch lets you find words by entering associated qualities and
definitions to find words you want. Select the WordSearch button to find
dictionary definitions containing the words you specify.

Type a single word, such as advertising, to search for associated words
and phrases, such as commercial, hype, and soft sell.

Enter more than one word to refine your search. Use AND, OR, or NOT
between each word from the convenient button interface. Use AND to
narrow your search or use OR to broaden your search or use NOT to narrow
your search.

Use WordSearch(TM) when the word you want is on the tip of your tongue
but you can't recall it.  Simply give it one or more "hints" and the
WordSearch instantly scans the entire dictionary,  presenting you with a
choice of words.  Use the WordSearch to stimulate ideas,  find facts,
or just to have fun!

THESAURUS - 500,000 Synonyms at Your Fingertips:

Also included is the complete Roget's Electronic Thesaurus,  with more
than 500,000 synonyms.  You can switch quickly between the dictionary
and thesaurus to get definitions for newly found synonyms.

More Power More Convenience:

New features include automatic lookup by copying a word from a document
into the clipboard to give you definitions or synonyms--or both at the
same time. Or use the "Browse List" to scroll through the entire
dictionary, word by word.  After you've found what you're looking for,
whether it's a single word or an entire definition, you can pasta it
directly into your document.

Wildcard - A Puzzle Lovers Best Friend:

The Wildcard feature finds words when you don't know all the letters.
For example, type "sl??p" and Wildcard gives you sleep, sloop, slump,
and slurp.

Anagram -  lets you find the other words hidden in the one you're
using.  Type "spot" and Anagram gives you opts, post, stop, and tops.

And much more...

Licensing and Prices:

o Single user node locked (individual)
o Site Licenses

The following information concerns additional license types which may be
of interest to you.

Individual and Volume Purchase Agreements:

Price: $49.95     

Site Licenses: Call for volume pricing.

A Site License is any individual site which is defined as a separate
postal address, whether a single business location or a building address
