This message is to announce the first community-wide meeting of the St
Cloud Area Linux Users Group.  For more current information, check out our
web site at http://www.cloudnet.com/~tomc/scalug.html. 
 
 
SCALUG's First Community-wide Meeting!
 
The first community-wide SCALUG meeting is scheduled for 6:30 PM, March
11th, in room 115 of the Engineering and Computer Center, St Cloud State
University. If you need directions, contact Tom Cross at tomc@kendeco.com
or 320-253-1020, or Jim Howatt at jhowatt@eeyore.stcloud.msus.edu or
320-255-4960.  For changes in the meeting location and/or time, please
check our web page at http://www.cloudnet.com/~tomc/scalug.html.
 
The purpose of the meeting will be to accomplish the following:
 
    * Introduce attendees to Linux.
    * Discuss why someone would want Linux on their PC.
    * Show off some of Linux's capabilities.
    * Determine from the attendees what topics subsequent meetings should
      cover.
 
The SCALUG meeting will consist of three parts.  First, a presentation
introducing Linux and it capabilities.  Second, a question-answer
session covering Linux and third, a general discussion.  
 
If you are a seasoned Linux user, please come to the meeting regardless of
the focus on introducing Linux.  After the presentation, we would like to
get a feel for how many Linux users there are in the St Cloud area and
what kind of topics we should schedule for future meetings.

- -------------------------------------------------------------------------
General Information about SCALUG

SCALUG is a loosely knit group of Linux enthusiasts in the St Cloud, MN
area.  This group started in mid 1996 by meeting weekly at a local
restaurant in St Cloud.  SCALUG is now planning on expanding to more
formal meetings, focusing on certain topics. 

SCALUG has two mailing lists.  One is an annoucement only list and the
other is a general discussion list.  You do not have to be from the St
Cloud area or an "active" SCALUG member to join!  Try them out! 

For more current information regarding SCALUG, check out our web page at
http://www.cloudnet.com/~tomc/scalug.html.

- ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
Meeting Information

We have two types of meetings, informal and formal.  We meet weekly at a
local restaurant for general, informal discussions and irregular formal
meetings that are announced here. 

Weekly Meetings

The SCALUG group meets every Friday from Noon to 1:30 PM.  We are
currently meeting at the Dong Khanh Buffet lcoated at 1004 Division
Street, St Cloud, MN.  This location is not permanent.  Check the web site 
(http://www.cloudnet.com/~tomc/scalug.html) for changes in the meeting
location or time. If you would like to suggest a different location, 
subscribe to the SCALUG general discussion list and post your suggestion!

Formal Meetings 

SCALUG has irregular formal meetings that will be announced here.  The
formal meetings will have the same informal and relaxed atmospheres as the
informal meetings.  They will be called formal because they are more
widely announced and are focused on particular topics.  Check out web site
for our meeting schedule. 


Future Meeting Plans

After our first formal meeting, we will have a better idea of the number
of linux users in the area, and what topics they would be interested in. 
Some future meetings could include the following: 

   * Linux Installation Festival - Seasoned Linux users will be on hand to
     install Linux on new Linux users' computers. 
   * Setting up X windows for optimum performance 
   * Differnces in distributions - Just what are the differences between
     RedHat, Debian, and Slackware? 

If you have any suggestions for future topics, please subscribe to the
SCALUG general discussion mailing list and let us know!  If you would like
to help with doing presentations or with installation, let us know.

- ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
SCALUG Mailing Lists

SCALUG has two mailing lists, SCALUG Announce and SCALUG.  SCALUG Announce
is used for SCALUG announcements and the SCALUG list is used for general
discussion.  You do not have to be a SCALUG member to subscribe to either
mailing list.


SCALUG Announce Mailing list

The SCALUG Annouce mailing list is used to send SCALUG announcements to 
interested parties.  Announcements are typically about meetings and/or
local Linux resources being made available or discovered.  

To subscribe to the SCALUG Announce mailing list, send an e-mail message 
like the one below:  

     To:  SCALUG-Announce-Request@kendeco.com >
Subject:  subscribe 

   subscribe 


SCALUG General Discussion List 

The SCALUG General Discussion list is used for discussion of a wide
variety of topics including (but not restricted to) planning for SCALUG
meetings, installing Linux, using Linux, local Linux resources, and
general Linux experiences.

To subscribe to the SCALUG General Discussion list, send an e-mail message
like the one below: 

     To: SCALUG-Request@kendeco.com  
Subject:  subscribe

    subscribe 




