The new Linux Developers Resource CD set is great!! Everything you need,
all in one little box.  But six CDs is a little much to search when you
want to find one file.  

Infomagic includes great ls_lR files to help you,  but wouldn't a quick
and easier database search be better?  

Linux already has a file search engine called locate(1L).  It uses a 
database, built every morning at 7am (depending on your Crontab) to 
locate a file in no time flat.  Wouldn't it be nice if the CDs had the 
same thing?

So I made it.

Run the install script.  All it does is put the cd database in the right
place, and the script in the right place.  Note that this requires LOCATE,
though I suspect it comes with most (if not all) linices. (eek!) 
Now, you can just

   locatecd xpdf

and it will tell you the locations of all files with "xpdf" in it. 

The kits are located at http://www.cs.colostate.edu/locatecd/
Make sure you get the set that goes with the CD-Set that you have.

