The Linux Game SDK Project
		==========================


This is an announce for a project which aims at creating
a full development environment under Linux for professional
video games developers.

The primary goal is to provide an unified and easy to use
software API to access hardware acceleration features under
Linux: video hardware, sound (through the Linux kernel drivers),
input devices (joysticks, mouse, ...), but also higher level
parts like a 3D engine (probably based upon OpenGL) which will
use 3D acceleration hardware when present. It will also provide
an easy way to make networked games.

Please note this is a new project, currently at the design stage.
We are looking for developers that want to join in and help us.
We're planning to get material from existing projects that could
be helpful, so if you already have a similar project please consider
to share it with us ;)

A dedicated mailing list has been created so that we can discuss
how we'll work.

The primary Web page is http://www.essi.fr/~speter/gsdk.html, and
it contains more complete info about this project and how I thought
it would be. You will find there how to susbscribe to the GSDK 
mailing-list.

		Please help us make Linux the best OS for _all_
applications ! ;-)

