organization: Courts of Chaos Research Center
x-auth: PGPMoose V1.1 PGP comp.os.linux.announce
newsgroups: comp.os.linux.announce


-----BEGIN PGP SIGNED MESSAGE-----


pnews is a program that allows you to read news off-line with a
variety of existing newsreaders.

pnews uses suck to retrieve news, then spools it locally without using
INN or cnews.

pnews can be used with cron and diald to automate news retrieval.

Naturally, outgoing articles are spooled and sent out in batches as
well.

pnews stands for "personal news", and is not at all suited for a full
feed, its goal is comparatively simple setup and use.

You can get pnews at:

http://www.iquest.net/~jbuchana/computer.html

Version 0.13 is aimed mostly at maintenance and stability. There are a
couple of new features though.

New stuff:

1. There's a new field in the pnewsrc file. It's called
crosspost_tolerance, and it indicates the maximum number of newsgroups
that you mind an article being in. If you set it to -1, it does
nothing, if you set it to a positive integer, you won't see articles
that are crossposted to more than this number of groups.

2. pnews_make_sucknewsrc is a new program that will take your active
file, then read information about the newsgroups from your NNTP server
and use it to build an up-to-date sucknewsrc file. This is handy if
you don't want to read every article in a given group the next time
you run get_news.


Jim Buchanan        c22jrb@dawg.delcoelect.com         jbuchana@iquest.net
