[I (Russell Marks) don't have net access any more, but Steven has been
kind enough to upload wdbinfo on my behalf, and is also posting this
for me]

Wdbinfo reads workman database files and can give complete listings of
the contents of audio CDs described in them without ever needing to go
near the CDs themselves.

Here's the LSM entry:

- --------------------------- cut to the chase -----------------------------
Begin3
Title:          wdbinfo
Version:        1.0
Entered-date:   23NOV96
Description:    Wdbinfo extracts information from a workman database
		file. This is what many audio-CD-playing programs, not
		just workman, use to store information about audio
		CDs. It's only really used for storing names of tracks
		etc., but can also be used for determining the length
		of a CD and each track on it, so it's possible for
