-----BEGIN PGP SIGNED MESSAGE-----

Hello,

I've just put the new version 0.5 of netboot into sunsite's incoming. It
should soon appear as /pub/Linux/system/Linux-boot/netboot-0.5.tar.gz on
sunsite and it's mirrors. The major changes in this version are:

- - The development platform has been completely moved from DOS using
  Borland-C to Unix using the Dev86-tools from the ELKS project, which
  are freely available from tsx-11.mit.edu. You will now be able to
  compile everything under Linux. I also wrote a peephole optimizer,
  which makes bcc's output even smaller than what has been produced
  with Borland-C!

- - The DOS loader can now use a Unix directory to create a bootable DOS
  image. Also, the ramdisk driver has been changed so that it's now
  possible to remove the ramdisk under DOS, when it is no longer needed.
  It should now also be possible to boot Win95 with the DOS loader (I
  haven't tested it as I don't have Win95). The problem which caused
  the DOS driver to not correctly access floppy disks has also been
  fixed.

- - Thanks to Michael Riepe a PCB layout is now available for the FlashCard
  Flash-EPROM card.

Due to personal reasons I will not be able to do any further development
on netboot for the next 2 to 3 months. However, I will be able to receive
mail, and will help you out with problems or eventually produce a bug-fix
release as time permits.

gero.


