-----BEGIN PGP SIGNED MESSAGE-----

Hello all,

we have just finished xled v1.3, a multi-purpose digital counter utility 
for the X11 desktop. It's a small but useful utility, which 
can be used to display the number of new emails received, voice messages
received by the vbox package, or in fact any other value supplied
as the return value of a shell command.
If you use the vbox package, you might be familiar with xled, which has
been included in this package under the name of xvboxled. But we added
a lot of new features which make this program useful not only in
conjunction with vbox, so we decided to change the name and make it
available for a broader audience.
xled is available from from fb4-1112.uni-muenster.de /pub/ffwd
(will be uploaded to sunsite soon).


>From the xled README file:
- ---
xled (formerly called xvboxled) is an utility for the X11 desktop,
originally designed as an add-on to the vbox package, which uses the audio 
functions of an ISDN card to use your Linux box as an answering machine.
xled shows the number of new messages in the vbox incoming dir as a 
7-segment LED display on the X desktop. As of version 1.3, it can also
be used to show the number of mails in a mail spool file (e.g. as a 
replacement for xbiff) - hence the new name. Finally, it can be used to
monitor the exit status of any given shell command. Other new features
of version 1.3 include the option to flash the keyboard LEDs if a new 
voice- / email was received, acoustic feedback with the "-bell" option,
and a user-defineable number of digits to be displayed.
- ---


xled LSM entry follows:

